{
  "id": "COMPOUND:13623 - PROTEIN:4856",
  "verbalization": "Selgantolimod appears to have a shared target pathway with Magnesium levulinate, which in turn targets Botulinum neurotoxin type F. This suggests a potential indirect relationship where Selgantolimod may influence the activity of Magnesium levulinate, which then affects Botulinum neurotoxin type F. The evidence is consistent across three distinct paths, each linking Selgantolimod to a different target (Keratin, Plasma kallikrein, and Nucleoside diphosphate kinase A), all of which are subsequently targeted by Magnesium levulinate. This indicates that Selgantolimod may act through a common intermediary, Magnesium levulinate, to modulate Botulinum neurotoxin type F. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible regulatory or functional link between Selgantolimod and Botulinum neurotoxin type F, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be elucidated.",
